<title>UK: ING Barings appoints chief international economist.</title>
<headline>ING Barings appoints chief international economist.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>ING Barings has appointed Malcolm Roberts as chief international economist, reporting directly to John Reynolds, global head of research.</p>
<p>A statement said Roberts will be responsible for establishing an integrated research product for the OECD (Organisation for Economic Co-Operation and Development) and emerging countries.</p>
<p>He joins ING Barings from Credit Suisse. Prior to that he was at UBS Ltd and Salomon Brothers.</p>
<p>-- Caroline Allen, London newsroom +44 171 542 6414</p>
</text>
